i think there's a lot of rumor and a lot  of speculation um i'm sure that there  was time for the king to have  an audience in some capacity with harry  and megan i mean don't forget that  charles is very very keen to try and  smooth relations try and move things on  but i think any speculation that she  requested a meeting is probably just  that speculation but i think we can  safely assume given that they were over  here for well over a week there would  have been time for both of them to speak  with charles i think part of the success  of queen elizabeth as we are now  realizing because i think we took it for  granted for so long  was her  ability to be head of state to be head  of the church to be the monarch whilst  also being a wife  and a mother  and a grandmother and a  great-grandmother somehow she managed to  fulfill all of those roles  [Music]  [Applause]  i think for many people one of the most  moving spectacles of the funeral was the  lone piper pipe major paul burns who was  the queen's personal piper he would wake  her up at balmoral with 15 minutes of  pipe playing outside her bedroom window  he even played when she wasn't  in residence such was his devotion to  his monarch and  i think those  haunting pipes will stay with everyone  for a very long time in fact the queen  had the pipes play at the duke of  edinburgh's funeral  and she said  for her it was one of the most moving  parts of the day it will always stay  with her she said  [Music]
 

